<Defs>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SLIME_STREAM_ROWS_1 — four canal fill-tier ladders, one per colour.

       Same shape as the water/tar ladders in FlowWorks_Terrain.xml
       (ParentName WaterShallow, temporary=true, empty driesTo, canFreeze
       false — the flooded-cell contract every FluidDef.fillTerrain* field
       requires) — these are the CANAL side (what an excavated cell shows
       once RM_Fluid_Slime<Colour> pulses into it), distinct from the
       NATURAL body terrain (RM_Slime<Colour>Shallow/Deep) that
       Tools/generate_liquid_suite.py's LIQUID_ROWS table generates into
       Defs/LiquidTypes/TerrainDefs/ — a natural, non-excavated placement of
       THAT terrain is what auto-primes a reservoir
       (RM_MapComponent_Excavation.IsSourceCell reads any natural cell whose
       TerrainDef.IsWater is true, i.e. carries the vanilla `Water` tag,
       which WaterShallow already does and this file's ParentName inherits,
       as a limitless source — no new C#).

       pathCost per tier matches RM_Fill_Tar_* exactly (200/300/300,
       Trace left at WaterShallow's own inherited 30) — slime is the SAME
       Heavy viscosityClass as tar on the wade axis; what makes it read as
       thicker still is the canal fluid's own ticksPerTile (480 vs tar's
       360, FlowWorks_Fluids.xml), not a heavier wade cost invented fresh.

       Colours are tints of vanilla's own WaterShallowRamp/WaterDeepRamp —
       no new art, the same "colour with material" convention this mod
       already uses for RM_Water_<Colour> (Defs/ManyWaters/TerrainDefs/
       RM_ColoredWater.xml) and RM_Fill_Tar_* above. WHITE and YELLOW reuse
       ManyWaters' own already-authored "Chalk"/"Amber-adjacent" tint
       values rather than inventing new ones from nothing.
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <!-- ── RED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallow">
    <defName>RM_Fill_SlimeRed_Trace</defName>
    <label>shallow channel, red slime</label>
    <description>A channel carrying a trace of red slime — already thick enough to cling.</description>
    <temporary>true</temporary>
    <driesTo></driesTo>
    <canFreeze>false</canFreeze>
    <color>(168,40,40)</color>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallow</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallowStill</li>
      <li>Flood</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallow">
    <defName>RM_Fill_SlimeRed_Half</defName>
    <label>half-full channel, red slime</label>
    <description>A channel filling with red slime to about half its depth.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterChestDeepRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterChestDeepRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <temporary>true</temporary>
    <driesTo></driesTo>
    <canFreeze>false</canFreeze>
    <color>(168,40,40)</color>
    <pathCost>200</pathCost>
    <extraDraftedPerceivedPathCost>60</extraDraftedPerceivedPathCost>
    <extraNonDraftedPerceivedPathCost>320</extraNonDraftedPerceivedPathCost>
    <renderPrecedence>395</renderPrecedence>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallow</li>
      <li>WaterFreshShallowStill</li>
      <li>Flood</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

